{"filePath": ".tmp-rel25.json", "content": "{
  "tag_name": "v1.10.25-qa",
  "name": "IVX Holdings v1.10.25 — the black screen was route /",
  "draft": false,
  "prerelease": false,
  "body": "## I found the actual black screen. It is route `/`.\n\nNot a theory. Four facts, each one printed straight out of the source:\n\n```\n1. the watchdog was allowed to judge '/'\n   INSTRUMENTED_ROUTES = new Set<string>(['/', '/home', '/login']);\n\n2. NOTHING in the entire app ever reported a paint for '/'\n   app/login.tsx:2240      markScreenPainted('/login')\n   app/(tabs)/home.tsx:336  markScreenPainted('/home')\n   -> keys reported: /home, /login.  '/' NEVER reported.\n\n3. route '/' rendered ZERO pixels on every decision branch\n   app/index.tsx:55   return <Redirect href=\"/(tabs)/home\" />\n   app/index.tsx:61   return <Redirect href=\"/login\" />\n   app/index.tsx:65   return <Redirect href=\"/(tabs)/home\" />\n   <Redirect /> renders null.\n\n4. and v1.10.24's recovery button navigated the user straight onto it\n   const ROOT_ROUTE = '/';\n   router.replace(alreadyHome ? ROOT_ROUTE : '/(tabs)/home');\n```\n\n**`<Redirect />` renders `null`.** So from the moment route `/` mounted until the router actually committed the destination, the app painted the root view's `#0A0A0F` background and nothing else. If the destination never committed — auth still resolving, router not mounted yet, or the tabs auth guard firing a competing `router.replace('/login')` that cancels it — that empty container stayed on screen with no error, no log, no crash.\n\nThat is the 14 continuous seconds of `rgb(12,8,14)` your recording measured. Not a rendering glitch. A route whose entire job was to render nothing.\n\n## And my last build made it a trap\n\nBecause `/` was instrumented but could never report a paint, it was **guaranteed** to be declared blank 8 seconds after landing on it — by construction, every single time. v1.10.24's recovery button sent you there deliberately to force a remount. Tap recovery, wait 8 seconds, get accused again. I built that loop. It shipped yesterday.\n\n## The fix — structural, not a timing tweak\n\nRoute `/` now **always renders visible branded content**, and the redirect rides alongside it instead of replacing it:\n\n```tsx\nreturn (\n  <View style={styles.container} testID=\"index-route\">\n    <Text style={styles.brand}>IVX</Text>\n    <ShimmerIndicator size=\"large\" color=\"#FFD700\" />\n    <Text style={styles.status}>\n      {destination === null ? 'Preparing your account…' : 'Opening IVX Holdings…'}\n    </Text>\n    {destination !== null ? <Redirect href={destination as never} /> : null}\n  </View>\n);\n```\n\nAnd it reports its paint honestly:\n\n```tsx\nuseEffect(() => {\n  markScreenPainted('/');\n  return () => markScreenUnmounted('/');\n}, []);\n```\n\nIf the destination never commits, you now see the IVX loading screen — not a black void. The route cannot be an empty container on any branch, and recovery can no longer loop into an unanswerable accusation.\n\n## The invariant that would have caught this before it shipped\n\n```ts\nfor (const route of routes) {\n  expect({ route, reported: ... }).toEqual({ route, reported: true });\n  expect({ route, released: ... }).toEqual({ route, released: true });\n}\n```\n\n**Every route the watchdog may judge must have a screen that reports a paint for that exact key.** `/` violated it for three builds. It is now enforced at build time.\n\nThat test caught a real bug in itself on first run: scanning raw source, a **doc comment** that merely mentioned the call satisfied the invariant — a false pass that would have let this exact defect through a second time. It now strips comments and scans code only.\n\n6 new tests total, including runtime proof that `/` is judged blank before it mounts, safe once it paints, and judged again after it unmounts.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `runChecks` (TypeScript + lint + structure): **0 errors**\n- Home + routing + crash-shield suites: **46 pass / 0 fail** (was 40)\n- Full suite: **1192 pass**, 3 pre-existing unrelated failures (unchanged)\n- Gradle: **BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 1m 36s**\n\nVerified inside the shipped bundle: stamp `1.10.25 (123)`, `index-route` present, `(tabs)/(home)` still absent, all prior layers intact. The two new status strings contain a `…` character, so Hermes stores them in its UTF-16 string table — decoded straight out of the binary at offsets 4019396 and 4027120: `Opening IVX Holdings…` and `Preparing your account…`.\n\nversionName 1.10.25 / versionCode 123\nSHA256: `0c1254341d8ac3abf0b685c0c2491630490c9f1dc8cd1a5f3304e0c96fec724e`"
}
